From ae81f57dfe725c084fb73c96b1296507e0b29a89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:50:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 0201: true liquid glass, flat outfit grid with real renders
 and Chinese names

Glass: the tint now lives inside .glassEffect(.regular.tint(...)) so the
intensity slider drives the glass itself (clear and refractive at low
values, milkier at high ones). The 0194 solid fill overlay sat on top of
the glass and turned the panel into frosted plastic; the slider only
faded that white wash, so the glass never visibly changed.

Outfits: the stacked deck is replaced by a flat scrollable grid (the
user's mockup layout: title, subtitle, four columns, foil background,
gold border on the worn one). Cards show a real 3D render
(of_<character>_<ItemName>.png, Blender) above the Chinese name from
the game's ItemCloth.msbt. A plain Button tap selects now: the deck's
tap-to-select never fired because DragGesture's default minimumDistance
is 10pt, so a stationary tap never activated the gesture and the pick
always stayed default. The hero is gone from this tab; the character
is named in the grid title and picked from the cards below.
---
